//? Title: Christofides' TSP Construction: Parity, Euler Walks and Shortcuts
//? Subtitle: Actual stage records, conditional approximation guarantees and bounded subset matching
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A delivery route must visit every location and return to its start, while keeping
its total distance small. Searching every order soon becomes impractical.
For symmetric metric costs, Christofides' construction combines a minimum
spanning tree, a minimum perfect matching of its odd-degree vertices, and
Euler-walk shortcutting to obtain a tour within 3/2 of the optimum in exact
arithmetic. We inspect the actual native stages on five vertices, retain the
original square, verify a controlled family, and expose both nonmetric failures
and the exponential matching limit of this bounded implementation.
)

\toc

> Five vertices: fix parity, then remove repeated visits

Vertex 0 is a hub and vertices 1–4 are interchangeable leaves. Every hub/leaf
cost is 1; every distinct leaf/leaf cost is 1.5. These complete costs obey the
triangle inequality: a leaf pair costs 1.5≤1+1 through the hub. The drawing is
a schematic of these costs, not a planar Euclidean embedding.

The minimum spanning tree contains the four hub spokes and costs 4. Its hub
has even degree four and all four leaves have odd degree one. Pairing leaves
(1,2) and (3,4) costs 3 and makes every multigraph degree even. The actual
Euler walk repeats the hub; keeping only each vertex's first visit and then
closing the cycle shortens its cost from 7 to 6.5. All stage values below come
from one execution of the canonical kernel.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/christofides_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto d=dm::algorithms::hub_tsp_distances(4);
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::christofides_trace(d);
  if(!dm::algorithms::is_tsp_metric(d) || t.result.cost!=6.5 || t.euler_cost!=7)return 1;
  std::print("| stage | actual edges or order | cost |\n| :--- | :--- | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& [u,v,w]:t.tree)std::print("| tree edge | {}--{} | {} |\n",u,v,w);
  for(const auto& [u,v,w]:t.matching)std::print("| matching edge | {}--{} | {} |\n",u,v,w);
  std::print("| Euler circuit | {} | {} |\n| first visits, then close | {} | {} |\n",t.euler_vertices,t.euler_cost,t.result.tour,t.result.cost);
  std::print("\nOdd tree vertices: {}. Retained Euler positions: {}. Edge identities consumed: {}.\n",t.odd_vertices,t.kept_positions,t.work.euler_edge_visits);
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(60,1100);
  const std::array<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint,5> points{{{0,0},{-2,0},{0,2},{2,0},{0,-2}}};
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;stroke.color={71,85,105};stroke.width=3;
  for(const auto& [u,v,w]:t.tree)diagram.path({points[u],points[v]},stroke);
  stroke.color={37,99,235};
  for(const auto& [u,v,w]:t.matching)diagram.path({{points[u].x+10,points[u].y},{points[v].x+10,points[v].y}},stroke);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.circle=true;node.width=0.85;node.height=0.85;node.font_size=20;
  for(int panel=0;panel<2;++panel)for(std::size_t v=0;v<points.size();++v) {
    node.fill=std::ranges::find(t.odd_vertices,v)!=t.odd_vertices.end()?dm::graphics::RGB{254,240,138}:dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254};
    diagram.node(std::format("p{}v{}",panel,v),{points[v].x+10*panel,points[v].y},std::format("{}",v),node);
  }
  diagram.text({0,3.6},std::format("Tree cost {}",t.tree_cost),22)
      .text({10,3.6},std::format("Odd matching cost {}",t.matching_cost),22)
      .text({5,5.2},"Actual graph stages; gold vertices have odd tree degree",20);
  node.circle=false;node.width=13.5;node.height=1.6;node.fill={239,246,255};
  diagram.node("euler",{5,-5.2},std::format("Actual Euler walk, cost {}\n{}",t.euler_cost,t.euler_vertices),node);
  node.fill={220,252,231};
  diagram.node("tour",{5,-8.7},std::format("First visits + closing start, cost {}\n{}",t.result.cost,t.result.tour),node)
      .edge("euler","tour","shortcut repeated hub")
      .save_svg("build/christofides_method.svg");
}
```
