\caption(The original rounded-diagonal square and native Euclidean control both cost four. Parallel matching/tree copies retain distinct identities.)
\alttext(Four labelled unit-square vertices form the recorded directed cycle 0 to 3 to 2 to 1 to 0. Gold vertex zero marks the start and finish.)

A multigraph matters even in the two-vertex control: its single tree edge and
matching edge share endpoints, but both must be traversed. The trace's Euler
edge ids refer to tree edges followed by matching edges; they never collapse
parallel copies into one undirected endpoint pair.

> Exact matching here means exponential subset search

For a subset S of odd vertices, take its smallest vertex i and try each partner
j in S. The recurrence is

$$
D(\varnothing)=0,\qquad
D(S)=\min_{j\in S\setminus\{i\}}\{d(i,j)+D(S\setminus\{i,j\})\}.
$$
\alttext(The best perfect matching pairs the smallest remaining vertex with each possible partner and combines its edge cost with the best matching of the remaining subset.)

Only even masks have solutions. The implementation evaluates each nonempty
even mask once, keeps the first smallest partner on a tie, and reconstructs its
selected pairs. For k≥2 even odd vertices, the actual table has 2^k entries,
2^(k−1)−1 nonempty even masks, and

$$
\sum_{\substack{s=2\\s\text{ even}}}^{k}\binom{k}{s}(s-1)
=(k-2)2^{k-2}+1
$$
\alttext(The total partner relaxations over all even masks equal k minus two times two to the power k minus two, plus one.)

partner relaxations. The identity follows by subtracting the count of nonempty
even subsets from the sum of their cardinalities, k·2^(k−2).
Odd masks occupy storage but have no relaxations. The trace records these
actual counts; the plot transforms them with log2 for a readable vertical scale.
It does not measure runtime.

For a hub with k even leaves, spoke cost 1 and rim cost 1.5, the MST is the star
and exactly those k leaves are odd. Any Hamiltonian cycle has two spokes and
k−1 leaf edges, so OPT=2+1.5(k−1). This family verifies the counting formula
and a known optimum without implementing a second solver in the report.
All these tours attain the optimum; the family does not test tightness of the
worst-case 3/2 bound.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/christofides_matching_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> k_values,table_log,partner_log;
  std::print("| vertices | odd k | table entries | even masks | partner relaxations | predicted partners | tour | known OPT |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t k=2;k<=16;k+=2) {
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::christofides_trace(dm::algorithms::hub_tsp_distances(k));
    const auto predicted=(k-2)*(std::size_t{1}<<(k-2))+1;const double optimum=2+1.5*(k-1);
    if(t.odd_vertices.size()!=k || t.work.matching_candidates!=predicted || t.result.cost!=optimum)return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k+1,k,t.work.matching_table_entries,t.work.matching_masks,t.work.matching_candidates,predicted,t.result.cost,optimum);
    k_values.push_back(k);table_log.push_back(std::log2(t.work.matching_table_entries));partner_log.push_back(std::log2(t.work.matching_candidates));
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(k_values,table_log,"table",{37,99,235},1.5).points(k_values,table_log,"table",{37,99,235},4)
      .line(k_values,partner_log,"partners",{234,88,12},1.5).points(k_values,partner_log,"partners",{234,88,12},4)
      .legend({"allocated table entries","actual partner relaxations"},{{37,99,235},{234,88,12}})
      .title("Exact subset matching grows with the odd set")
      .x_label("odd tree vertices k").y_label("log2(actual count)").x_limits(1,17).y_limits(-1,21)
      .save_svg("build/christofides_matching_work.svg");
  std::vector<std::pair<double,double>> line;for(int i=0;i<64;++i)line.emplace_back(i,0);
  const auto long_line=dm::algorithms::christofides_trace(dm::algorithms::euclidean_tsp_distances(line));
  if(long_line.result.cost!=126 || long_line.odd_vertices.size()!=2)return 1;
  std::print("\n64-vertex line: {} odd vertices, {} matching table entries, cost {} = twice the endpoint distance.\n",long_line.odd_vertices.size(),long_line.work.matching_table_entries,long_line.result.cost);
  constexpr std::size_t largest_table=std::size_t{1}<<22;
  std::print("At the supported k=22 limit: {} table slots; long-double cost plus byte-choice payload on this platform is {} bytes (excluding other storage).\n",largest_table,largest_table*(sizeof(long double)+sizeof(std::uint8_t)));
}
```
